      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 96, hedge shrub, the 'Red Robin' hybrid of Photinia glabra and P. serratifolia. Two care sources only (NC State and the RHS cultivar page); no Missouri BG or Clemson page found and ASPCA has no photinia entry. Size: RHS 4 to 8 m by 2.5 to 4 m after 10 to 20 years, NC State 10 to 20 ft by 10 to 15 ft; 600 by 300 cm is the agent's mapping. Hardiness not stored: the RHS page read does not show the H value in its text; NC State USDA 7 to 9. Toxicity: no source grades it; RHS says the fruit is not to be eaten and advises gloves and mentions pets (fruit not to be eaten), which is not a grade, so status unknown and pets show unknown. Pruning in late spring gives a new red flush but removes the flowers (NC State), RHS suggests light pruning when the first colour fades. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
